---
layout: default
---
{%- comment %}
  Publications page layout — Direction A.
  Header pattern (eyebrow + h1 + lead + network bg) → year-grouped paper rows
  rendered via jekyll-scholar (group_by: year, descending — see _config.yml).
  Technical reports follow as a flush sub-section.
  No stats strip, no filter chips, no preview thumbnails.
{% endcomment -%}

{%- capture pub_count -%}{% bibliography_count -f papers %}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- assign pub_count = pub_count | strip -%}

{%- capture eyebrow_html -%}
PUBLICATIONS · {{ pub_count }} ENTRIES · 2016 — 2026
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- capture lead_html -%}
Over a decade of multidisciplinary work modelling data-rich complex systems: from network
science and epidemics to human mobility, nutrition, the science of science and more.
{%- endcapture -%}

{% include page_header.liquid
   net="publications"
   eyebrow=eyebrow_html
   title="Peer-reviewed work."
   lead=lead_html %}

<section class="section section--flush pubs">
  <div class="wrap">
    {% bibliography -f papers %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tight pubs pubs--reports">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="reports-head">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--accent">§ — Notes</p>
      <h2 class="section-head__title">Technical reports.</h2>
    </header>
    <div class="pubs__reports-list">
      {% bibliography -f reports --group_by none %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
